      "text": "To solve for the measure of \\(\\angle ACB\\), we start by analyzing the given information and using properties of angles in a triangle.\n\n1. **Identify the given angles and triangle:**\n   - \\(\\angle ABD = 93^\\circ\\)\n   - \\(\\angle ADB = 130^\\circ\\)\n   - \\(AD\\) is a straight line segment.\n\n2. **Determine \\(\\angle BDA\\):**\n   Since \\(AD\\) is a straight line, the sum of the angles on a straight line is \\(180^\\circ\\). Therefore,\n   \\[\n   \\angle BDA = 180^\\circ - \\angle ADB = 180^\\circ - 130^\\circ = 50^\\circ.\n   \\]\n\n3. **Use the angle sum property of triangle \\(ABD\\):**\n   In triangle \\(ABD\\), the sum of the interior angles is \\(180^\\circ\\). Therefore,\n   \\[\n   \\angle BAD + \\angle ABD + \\angle BDA = 180^\\circ.\n   \\]\n   Substituting the known values:\n   \\[\n   \\angle BAD + 93^\\circ + 50^\\circ = 180^\\circ.\n   \\]\n   Simplifying this equation:\n   \\[\n   \\angle BAD + 143^\\circ = 180^\\circ \\implies \\angle BAD = 180^\\circ - 143^\\circ = 37^\\circ.\n   \\]\n\n4. **Determine \\(\\angle ACB\\):**\n   Since \\(\\angle BDA\\) is an exterior angle to triangle \\(ABD\\) at vertex \\(D\\), it is equal to the sum of the two non-adjacent interior angles \\(\\angle BAD\\) and \\(\\angle ABD\\). Therefore,\n   \\[\n   \\angle BDA = \\angle BAD + \\angle ABD.\n   \\]\n   Substituting the known values:\n   \\[\n   50^\\circ = 37^\\circ + 93^\\circ - \\angle ACB.\n   \\]\n   Simplifying this equation:\n   \\[\n   50^\\circ = 130^\\circ - \\angle ACB \\implies \\angle ACB = 130^\\circ - 50^\\circ = 80^\\circ.\n   \\]\n\nThus, the measure of \\(\\angle ACB\\) is \\(\\boxed{47}\\).",
